    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb3b4a4a_09d2b57d",
        "filename": "baseboard/volteer/baseboard.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 601,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-22T21:02:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "3 bits (8 USB daughter board combos) should be plenty for single board variant.  Each variant can decode the DB_TYPE bits differently if needed. Variants are likely to select different TCPC/PPC chip combos, but once that happens the tcpc_config[] and ppc_ports[] will move into board/volteer/board.c (and the variant board.c)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 601,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 601,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "34f7a3a8c759fda84f2876b4b219033cdc5b6fa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8227435_044c0dfa",
        "filename": "baseboard/volteer/baseboard.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 601,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-23T08:55:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "my prediction is that there\u0027ll be a variant that will define a few bits for itself from the unused bits but otherwise share the definitions\nwith the baseboard.\n\ni don\u0027t think it\u0027s useful to squeeze this down to 3 bits today.\ntechnically, we already have 9 daughter board types, although\nonly 3 can mate in this slot.\n\ni\u0027m going to prefix everything with USB_DB instead of DB because\nwe might similarly need to identify the audio DB, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "fb3b4a4a_09d2b57d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 601,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 601,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "34f7a3a8c759fda84f2876b4b219033cdc5b6fa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3cfbb3a8_8ead7aed",
        "filename": "baseboard/volteer/baseboard.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 605,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-22T21:02:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we intend the FW_CONFIG bit allocation to be shared by all Volteer variants, then we should move these to baseboard.h.\nIf we want to allow each board variant to define it\u0027s own FW_CONFIG bits, then we should move this to board/volteer/board.c\n\nI prefer 1st option (share FW_CONFIG bits) until we\u0027re forced to do something different.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 601,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 605,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "34f7a3a8c759fda84f2876b4b219033cdc5b6fa7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
